<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    ROT_GUARDIAN_GROVES_1. The three RUT_LiveIngredient_* harvested from
    src/RimUtinni/RotSporeKit/Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/RUT_RotSporeKit_GuardianGroves.xml's
    guarded mushrooms — now carrying the live-prep pair.

    ROT_LIVE_PREPARATIONS_1 (ticket 5, M4) decorated all three with
    CompTemperatureRuinable (minSafeTemperature 8 C — a fridge ruins them)
    and CompLifespan (150000 ticks = 2.5 in-game days), plus tickerType
    Rare, without which neither comp ticks at all. Ban 4 therefore reaches
    the INGREDIENTS too: even raw cut flesh dies if delayed or
    refrigerated, so a grove harvest cannot be warehoused and brewed at
    leisure back home. Both comps are VANILLA on purpose — they hold on any
    install, with or without mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards.

    Both modExtensions are ticket 5's as well: RM_LivePrepExtension is the
    tag src/RimUtinni/RotSporeKit/selftest_live_prep.py enforces both comps
    against, and RM_TreasureMarkerExtension makes an ingredient one of the
    Rot's treasures for owner card 6's sale conscience. Each is MayRequire'd
    on its own <li> — an ungated modExtension whose class cannot resolve
    discards the WHOLE def.

    The recipes that turn these into teas and symbionts are
    Defs/RecipeDefs/RUT_RotSporeKit_LivePrepRecipes.xml. These three
    defNames are a handoff contract — do not rename them.

    No ingestible block on purpose: these are brewing ingredients, not food
    a colonist should eat raw off the shelf (same posture RUT_ChitinPlating
    already takes in RUT_RotSporeKit_Resources.xml). Low stackLimit and low
    MarketValue-per-unit but nonzero, matching card 1/M6's "keep yields low,
    darned hard to obtain" ruling — the plant's own harvestYield (3) is the
    real scarcity lever, this is just "don't let it stack into a warehouse".

    Placeholder texPaths only, reused from already-shipped RotSporeKit item
    art. Owed to the art pipeline: bespoke sprites for all three.
  -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RUT_LiveIngredient_AgelessCap</defName>
    <label>orlath cap flesh</label>
    <description>Freshly cut flesh from an ageless cap, still faintly warm. It has to reach a brewing vessel fast, or it's worthless.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>RotSporeKit/Things/Item/MushroomLog/MushroomlLog_a</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <stackLimit>10</stackLimit>
    <healthAffectsPrice>false</healthAffectsPrice>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>40</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>18</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.1</Mass>
      <Beauty>2</Beauty>
      <Flammability>0.5</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>2.0</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>Foods</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>ExoticMisc</li>
    </tradeTags>
    <tickerType>Rare</tickerType>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_TemperatureRuinable">
        <minSafeTemperature>8</minSafeTemperature>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Lifespan">
        <lifespanTicks>150000</lifespanTicks>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_LivePrepExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
        <preparationFamily>RotLivePrep</preparationFamily>
      </li>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_TreasureMarkerExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
        <treasureTag>RotTreasure</treasureTag>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

